  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your 1-point cards (Aces and Face cards) for the final push. If the total is at 28, a Face card is a guaranteed win. Don't play your '10s' when the total is high (over 20), as you will almost certainly overshoot the 29 limit and be forced to pass.\n\nThe 'Seven-Point Barrier': Many players hoard 7s and 8s. If you see an opponent play a low card (1 or 2) when the total is 20, they are likely trying to set up a '29' for their next turn. If you have a high card that takes it to 27 or 28, you 'pass' the opportunity to themâ€”sometimes it is better to play a 1 and take it to 21, forcing THEM to do the work.\n\nCard Counting: There are exactly 4 cards of each rank. If all four 9-cards have been played, you know that a total of 20 is 'safe' from a single-card sweep by anyone holding a 9. Use this information to safely play your higher cards without gifting a sweep to the next player.",
    Player: "Keep your 1-point cards (Aces and Face cards) for the final push. If the total is at 28, a Face card is a guaranteed win. Don't play your '10s' when the total is high (over 20), as you will almost certainly overshoot the 29 limit and be forced to pass.\n\nThe 'Seven-Point Barrier': Many players hoard 7s and 8s. If you see an opponent play a low card (1 or 2) when the total is 20, they are likely trying to set up a '29' for their next turn. If you have a high card that takes it to 27 or 28, you 'pass' the opportunity to themâ€”sometimes it is better to play a 1 and take it to 21, forcing THEM to do the work.\n\nCard Counting: There are exactly 4 cards of each rank. If all four 9-cards have been played, you know that a total of 20 is 'safe' from a single-card sweep by anyone holding a 9. Use this information to safely play your higher cards without gifting a sweep to the next player.",
