    basic: "Keep your 1-point cards (Aces and Face cards) for the final push. If the total is at 28, a Face card is a guaranteed win. Don't play your '10s' when the total is high (over 20), as you will almost certainly overshoot the 29 limit and be forced to pass.",
    intermediate: "The 'Seven-Point Barrier': Many players hoard 7s and 8s. If you see an opponent play a low card (1 or 2) when the total is 20, they are likely trying to set up a '29' for their next turn. If you have a high card that takes it to 27 or 28, you 'pass' the opportunity to themâ€”sometimes it is better to play a 1 and take it to 21, forcing THEM to do the work.",
    advanced: "Card Counting: There are exactly 4 cards of each rank. If all four 9-cards have been played, you know that a total of 20 is 'safe' from a single-card sweep by anyone holding a 9. Use this information to safely play your higher cards without gifting a sweep to the next player.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "In a 4-player game, teamwork isn't allowed, but you can intentionally 'set up' the player after you if you are far behind and want to stop the leader from winning a sweep.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'If the total is at 25, only a 4-card or four 1s can win. Check your hand for these specific outs.',
